{"type":"message","id":"ce9f50a0","parentId":"2ae9c0cc","timestamp":"2026-03-31T03:16:21.106Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need to respond as main agent. The user gave a system message showing a progress report from main agent at 09:01:18 GMT+8. Then they gave a heartbeat prompt. We need to read HEARTBEAT.md and follow it. The system message is not a user message but a system note? Actually the system message says \"System: [2026-03-31 09:01:18 GMT+8] 现在我来整理今天的项目进展汇报。\" That seems like a system-generated note (maybe from the main agent's own report). Then they give the heartbeat prompt.\n\nWe need to follow HEARTBEAT.md: check memory/heartbeat-state.json, see if anything needs attention. If nothing, reply HEARTBEAT_OK. If something, output conclusion and recommended action.\n\nWe just updated heartbeat-state.json to timestamp 1774926838 (which is 2026-03-31 11:13 AM Beijing time? Let's check: 1774926838 is seconds since epoch. Convert: 2026-03-31 11:13:58? Actually 1774926838 corresponds to 2026-03-31 11:13:58 UTC? Let's trust.\n\nNow we need to see if there is anything needing attention. According to HEARTBEAT.md, we should check:\n\n1. Look at memory/heartbeat-state.json\n2. Prioritize checking the item that has been longest unchecked and most valuable: calendar, email, mentions, weather.\n3. If no checkable item or not suitable to disturb, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\n\nWe have not checked calendar, email, mentions, weather recently. The lastChecks in heartbeat-state.json show:\n\n- email: 1774484880 (old)\n- calendar: 1774616480\n- weather: 1774425720\n- mentions: 1774485080\n- openclawProject: 1774858795 (recent)\n- heartbeat: 1774858795 (recent)\n\nSo email, calendar, weather, mentions are stale. According to HEARTBEAT.md, we should prioritize checking the item that has been longest unchecked and most valuable. The longest unchecked is email (1774484880) which is from 2026-03-26? Actually that's old. So we should check em